        <item>
            <title>3.23.4</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:14:49 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>234</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.23.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's New in 3.23.4</h2><ul></ul><p><strong>Improved</strong></p><ul><li>The file list stays fast with batches of up to 1,000 files, and photo previews appear sooner.</li><li>While files are renamed or sorted, the bar at the bottom shows the progress.</li><li>Folder sorting with your own folder rule uses the names you typed by hand.</li><li>Cloud AI tries again once when uploading a large file to the server takes too long.</li></ul><p><strong>Fixed</strong></p><ul><li>The file list no longer goes blank after jumping to the end of a large batch sorted into many folders.</li><li>Hidden "._" files that macOS leaves on external drives, network shares and zip archives are no longer added to AI Rename or Quick Rename.</li><li>When Cloud AI can't reach the server, for example because a VPN or firewall blocks it, the file says so instead of showing a technical error.</li><li>Switching folder sorting from Auto to your own rule asks again for file descriptions that failed before.</li><li>Parts of the original name that your rename rule keeps, such as a date, are kept even when a backup AI service names the file.</li><li>Activity shows the right AI service for every file in a large batch.</li></ul>
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://zushapp.com/releases/Zush-3.23.4.dmg" length="20152292" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="FydFGcCmP7O5usBcQNqk76NRFr8vUcVk/2qah/u3cu0ikx0QCrmIbxqtyACSbh25LLqZ8QUf7dH23eR4SZSBDQ=="/>
